report=f'''# PACK15 · completion report

**DONE / READY for bounded host-local engineering scope · v1.10.0.** 9/9 requirements PASS. Single agent Contractor → Builder → Verify; no independent audit or external publication.

Concrete artifact: `{a['file']}`, {a['bytes']} bytes ({a['bytes']/1048576:.2f} MiB), {a['files']} signed runtime files. Manifest `{a['manifestSha256']}`; complete package SHA `{a['packageSha256']}`. Detached expected.json and development-trust.json remain outside the package. Private Ed25519 signing key stays .local/pack15/development-key.pem mode0600, excluded from payload/source manifest and never printed or transferred. This signer is locally generated engineering identity, not official RtR release authority.

Bounded streaming format has exact canonical manifest, sorted regular-file inventory, byte counts/SHA and Ed25519 domain-separated signature. Two independently built manifests/full packets match exactly. Verifier rejects signature/key/revocation/context/expiry/sequence and required independent pin mismatches; path traversal/collisions/symlinks/source mutation, payload bit flips/truncation/trailing/footer/header/noncanonical data never become verified installations. Primary RFC8032 empty-message vector matches Node crypto, and its seed/public/signature are confirmed in the retained original RFC snapshot. PACK15 is not TUF: minimum sequence, trustworthy clock and independently chosen digest/policy are caller-managed; no remote metadata/rotation/threshold/secure bootstrap claim.

Installation checks actual package before staging and again while copying, syncs files/directories and atomically renames under an exclusive install lock. Existing slots are never overwritten; source/data/evidence remain separate. Installed inventory and reconstructed full wire hash are reverified before explicit start. Two host profiles start with external Node and declared storage policy; host-preview has no flight adapter, host-sitl never auto-connects. Installed server also refuses direct Node/npm startup before writers unless external trust, profile, expected digest, sizing workload and outside data root are supplied; it rechecks signature/bytes and observed capacity itself. This guard protects reviewed code startup and does not replace an independently trusted bootstrap verifier for unknown code.

Actual installed-package process/start/restart tests passed for both host profiles on {f['runtime']['platform']}/{f['runtime']['arch']}, Node {f['runtime']['node']}. External runtime/OS are not bundled or generically certified. Persisted policy mismatch is rejected and retains the original ledger, rather than silently replacing quota/floor. HeraHub proposal cannot launch and remains NOT_CHECKED; Linux is not claimed measured by this macOS test. No connect/upload/ARM/AUTO, parameter writes or device work occurred in this milestone.

Capacity model is a declared scenario. It compares per-file/record-count/mission/store limits, retained source and receiver copies, estimated journal plus possible legacy results, full partial checkpoint copies, concurrent export workspace, two software slots plus staging, protected metadata and 20 GiB host floor. Unknown observed space stays CAPACITY_UNKNOWN; insufficient space/quota is visible. Forecasts do not allocate capacity, measure captures/journal rates or guarantee future storage. Runtime intake/export guards and existing evidence preservation remain authoritative. Actual UI exports a scenario bound to its observedAt and package manifest; stale/offline/error resets previous status and export. No automatic cleanup or activation. The declared default scenario (4 retained missions × 200 files × 5 MiB assumed file bound, one partial checkpoint and one concurrent export) requires {default['bytes']['requiredFreeBytes']/1024**3:.2f} GiB free including the host floor/reserves. At {default['observedAt']}, {default['inputs']['freeBytes']/1024**3:.2f} GiB was observed, so default-sizing.json correctly reports INSUFFICIENT. This is a sizing assumption, not a measured capture rate; the smaller declared UI test scenario fits. No data was removed to make a scenario pass.

**{total} canonical checks PASS, 0 FAIL; {n} full unit/API tests, 0 skipped; syntax PASS.** Shared controls {counts['controls']['pass']}; deployment UI {counts['deploymentUI']['pass']}; geo UI regression {counts['geoUIRegression']['pass']}; actual software campaign {counts['actualPackage']['pass']}; actual preview/UI/history {counts['actualLive']['pass']}; public CLI {counts['actualCLI']['pass']}; kernel {counts['kernel']['pass']} and {counts['kernel']['notChecked']} NOT_CHECKED original external BOM availability. Current preview is healthy/disconnected, no active record or storage task. All 664 pre-existing mission/dataset/checkpoint/recipient files retain exact bytes, historic QGC and all five GEO14 records replay, and prior benchmark/recovery remain readable.

| Requirement | Evidence |
|---|---|
| P15-01 | Captured Node/RFC/TUF snapshots, three scoped Refinery definitions, SOT intent diff/kernel gate |
| P15-02 | Versioned signed profiles, package campaign external Node/runtime observation, HeraHub launch refusal |
| P15-03 | Pure boundary/arithmetic/quota/unknown tests, eight sizing criteria, actual-sizing.json |
| P15-04 | freeze.json, two-build identity, artifact.json and deterministic inventory/source-mutation corpus |
| P15-05 | RFC vector and signature/trust/expiry/rollback/pin/byte adversarial tests; actual CLI verify |
| P15-06 | Immutable publication/lock/reopen/tamper tests, direct-start denial, two profile start/restart and persisted-policy mismatch |
| P15-07 | Six viewport/offline/capacity/signature-failure UI tests, actual read-only page/screenshot/export |
| P15-08 | Actual artifact/installed slot and restarted preview, all preserved-byte/legacy/geo record checks |
| P15-09 | 72-fact SOT/digest/gate, exact reconstruction of prior 37-fact registry, full tests/source fingerprints and scratch cleanup |

VERIFY history is retained, excluded from canonical totals: initial Refinery metadata lacked capture.source and a case-exact Rollback span; gates failed loudly, definitions were corrected without modifying snapshots. Initial packaging whitelist omitted existing font license/QGC README; it correctly refused packaging. The first completed package/start campaign exposed a design gap in default direct npm start, which could choose a runtime path inside the software slot; added server-level mandatory external startup context, two regression tests and an actual direct-start refusal, then rebuilt/repeated all package/runtime/UI/full checks. Prior candidate package and its slot remain as an internal audit artifact (attempt02), not the current deployment. One new-unit invocation in the default sandbox failed loopback listen EPERM; authorized loopback execution passed all tests. No automatic approval review rejection or permission pause.

SOT only appends INTENT.PACK15; 72 facts, digest 9cd670ebbfb94eb4. No hardware/signing authority/field-quality promotion. Official key ownership/rotation, independent security review/secure bootstrap, observed deployment platforms, native/HIL/field acceptance and human A/B remain separately gated. Next hardware-free work: secure bootstrap/key ownership and rotation contract with independent review, followed by signed release workflow; HeraHub integration awaits its observed runtime/configuration/SDK.

Cleanup: kernel scratch `{k['scratch_removed']}` removed; all .local pack15 unit/smoke/rebuild fixtures and browser fixture roots removed. No dependency install, whole-project/tmp copy or extra build directory. Current compact signed package and two measured software slots deliberately retained; existing flight/data evidence preserved. Private development key stays protected locally. Fixed Docker image reused, image prune only (no container/volume pruning). No external release.
''';(r/'delivery/COMPLETION-PACK15.md').write_text(report)
